hls: a finished playlist's init section failure is its segment's

0101 makes a live playlist's initialization section failure one of the
segment it maps: retried seg_max_retry times, then skipped or final as
seg_skip decides. A finished (VOD) playlist returned the error at once,
while the same playlist's own segment failures are retried and skipped:
a 503 once on the init section ended the input at the open, and a
segment that maps a missing section ended playback there (with 0109 and
0074, for good).

Take the same path on a finished playlist: segment_failure_is_final()
decides after the retries (with seg_skip=live a finished playlist's
failure is final, as for its segments). The skip still drops the skipped
segment's early open (http_multiple), so the next segment due is asked
for, not read from that connection.

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -2260,11 +2260,12 @@ restart:
 
         /* load/update Media Initialization Section, if any */
         ret = update_init_section(v, seg);
-        if (ret < 0 && !v->finished) {
-            /* On a live playlist, the initialization section's failure is
-             * one of the segment it maps: retried, skipped and failed for
-             * good as the segment's own would be (seg_max_retry, seg_skip,
-             * live_reload_timeout). The next segment asks for it again.
+        if (ret < 0) {
+            /* The initialization section's failure is one of the segment it
+             * maps: retried, skipped and failed for good as the segment's
+             * own would be (seg_max_retry, seg_skip, live_reload_timeout),
+             * on a finished playlist as on a live one. The next segment asks
+             * for it again.
              * An interrupt is none, also when the callback has dropped by
              * now: the section is asked for again on the next call. */
             if (ret == AVERROR_EXIT || ff_check_interrupt(c->interrupt_callback))
